{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mixed model network analysis chain mixed model network analysis chain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","fileName":"Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 18:30\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Network AI Application Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Network AI Application Architecture","ainetworkingcookbook.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"mixed model network analysis chain mixed model network analysis chain","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","fileName":"Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain","heading":"Mixed-Model Network Analysis Chain","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A mixed-model network analysis chain assigns successive stages of a workflow to different models. A local model can perform a private first-pass inspection, while a hosted model receives a bounded intermediate result for deeper explanation or recommendation.\n\nThe chain makes cost, privacy, and capability tradeoffs explicit, but each handoff can lose or distort information. Intermediate schemas and checks should define what one stage must produce for the next. Sensitive raw configuration should not cross the hosted boundary merely because a later chain component is easier to call.","tags":["baby"],"links":["